{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/399664-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-actual-play-part-6","id":399664,"title":"Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga (Actual Play) Part 6","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-09T18:31:31-08:00","id":399664,"title":"Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga (Actual Play) Part 6","content":"The Kiddie Pool Saga Continues!<br /> <br /> Previous Chapters and Character Portraits can be found here [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\">LINK</a>]<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Backstory</u></b><br /> <br /> 1. At a recent Elysium, Alice and I caught the tail end of a conversation between Earl Gossett (neonate, carthian, gangrel.) and the Peter (youngish elder, mekhet, invictus.) Earl was being somewhat rude to Peter in open Elysium.<br /> <br /> Earl Gossett: &quot;You can't tell me what to do!&quot; I never found out what the conflict was about, only that Earl was mouthing off to Peter.<br /> <br /> 2. Eve Liebsch (gangrel, aspiring Invictus, kiddie pooler) had recently asked a favor of Alice and me. She wanted us to store some documents of hers in our haven. As Eve still lives in the trial area, her haven is not officially recognized by the city and therefore not protected by law. Our haven has no such limitations. We agree to store her documents. In payment, Eve hands us a document which appears to be a signed, transferrable boon from Michael Seville.<br /> <br /> I put them in our safe and thought nothing more of it. I didn't even peek. I was after all executing a boon.<br /> <br /> 3. The core of Baltimore is surrounded by 4 neighborhoods which are populated to varying degrees by vampires. Most of them are vassals of Baltimore, but not citizens. One such neighborhood lies to the SouthWest of Baltimore, and is populated by Carthians who are lead by a Council.<br /> <br /> Alice and I recently visited what passes for Elysium over there and witnessed some violence nearby. Roy (ventrue) whose territory is north of the council and west of Baltimore arrived with a small posse and had fisticuffs with a coterie of apparent high school aged vampires. Roy's group won the battle and took a prisoner.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>A Request from the Prince</u></b><br /> <br /> One fine evening, Alice and I are met near our haven by one of the Mekhet of the city. It is Diana (neonate, crone, childe of the archon Helen.) She informs us that there is Mekhet business to attend, and leads us to the west end of Baltimore. We meet in an elementary school gymnasium in the barrens which separate Baltimore from Council territory.<br /> <br /> We are soon joined by the following Mekhet:<br /> <br /> Kyle (childe of the archon Simon, Ordo Dracul Slave)<br /> Pascal Stitcher (neonate, carthian, childe of the archon Simon)<br /> The Archon Simon (lancea sanctum)<br /> Lucien Du Lac<br /> <br /> Simon looks at Diana and asks why she didn't bring Terry (mekhet, carthian.) They have some words and Diana leaves to get Terry.<br /> <br /> <b>Kyle Speaks:</b> &quot;I have acquired some actionable intel. Later tonight, the coterie of Roy's prisoner will trespass into Roy's territory and attempt to rescue the prisoner.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Simon:</b> &quot;None of you are required to participate in this operation, but the Prince requests that you intercept the intruders and prevent them from achieving their goals. You are encouraged to be malicious in the carrying out of this mission. If in the course of violence, you accidently destroy one of the offending vampires, your punishment will be light.&quot;<br /> <br /> I was a bit shocked that the Prince would issue a request instead of an order, but we readily agreed to participate. About this time, Diana returned with Terry and we filled them in on the situation.<br /> <br /> Kyle told us that we had a few hours before the incursion was likely, and we took that time to visit Kade and Lorraine. Kade has completed his mission for the Ordo Dracul that required him to keep a haven in the East side, and has since moved to the territory of his Sire, Sharon Winter. His haven is fairly close to Roy's territory. In the event that we are caught out near dawn, Kade has agreed to shelter us from the sun.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>The Mission</u></b><br /> <br /> Next, we travel to Roy's territory where the prisoner is being kept. From there, we divide into three groups and put eyes on the most likely routes to the prisoner. The rescue team shows up and we beat them up. Badly. The rescue team consists of:<br /> <br /> Mike (daeva)<br /> Jenny (daeva)<br /> Missy (daeva)<br /> Sherry (daeva)<br /> <br /> All four are Carthians, and the girls are all childer of Mike, who is the childer of the Prisoner (I never got his name.) During interrogation, we learn that Jenny and Missy are blood bound to Mike, who is blood bound to his sire. Sherry has somehow avoided the blood bond by convincing Mike that she drank from him while he slept, and is blood bound. Anyway, this is a familiar story. Boy gets embraced and decides to pass the embrace on to some cute girls he knows from high school.<br /> <br /> Before we leave, we wipe their memories of what happened. As far as they are concerned, they came to rescue the prisoner, got the shit kicked out of them by shadowy figures, and woke up in an abandoned building suffering grievous wounds.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Broken Glass</u></b><br /> <br /> I have learned something about Michael Seville (noseratu priscus.) He seems to try his best to keep the boon debt of neonates at manageable levels. However, he will not allow a neonate to become a creditor of his. Well, Alice and I were a bit in debt to Seville, so when we came into possession of the boon from Michael Seville we felt it would be in poor taste to use it to ask for a favor. Instead, we asked to apply it to our debt. Soon after, Seville offered us information which he assured us we would find valuable in exchange for a minor boon. Seville warned us that there would be an attack on our haven some time soon.<br /> <br /> With this information, Alice and I made preparations. First, we switched our day ghouls (steve and eddie) to a night schedule. Second, Alice and I made it a point to dress up and leave our haven only to double back under cloak of obfuscate and watch from a nearby rooftop. About a week later, the following events took place.<br /> <br /> 1. We noticed a vampire loitering in an alley across from our haven. The vampire in question is named Angela. She is formerly from Council territory, but has recently joined the kiddie poolers and is attempting to gain citizenship in Baltimore. She is met by a cargo van. They exchange a few words and the cargo van drives to the back of the house.<br /> <br /> 2. Miles (daeva, carthian) and Johnathan Poole (daeva, carthian) show up. They have fisticuffs, and Miles wins. Miles then pulls Angela away from our haven. They have words and Angela leaves with Miles.<br /> <br /> 3. Meanwhile, in the rear of the house the van has disgorged four armed assailants who are breaking into our home using a hydraulic jack and acetaline torches.<br /> <br /> 4. We follow them inside, obfuscated. They walk right into our ambush. There is only 1 survivor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Interrogation</u></b><br /> <br /> Using magic powers, we interrogate the surviving assailant. He was sent here by &quot;the Dark Lord&quot; to steal some documents. He is a blood slave (not even a ghoul) who is under the impression that the &quot;Dark Lord&quot; will make him immortal one day. Well, unless the Dark Lord is interested in my utility bills, I surmised that it was Eve's documents they were after.<br /> <br /> Further investigation went like so:<br /> <br /> 1. Alice is able to pull an image from the mind of the blood slave. The Dark Lord is a vampire whom we have seen before. His name is Joe, and he is a member of the Council who governs the territory to the SW.<br /> <br /> 2. Eve felt a little bad about the attack on our haven and told us we could look at the documents. The documents turn out to be a ledger of boons. Not only the boons directly involving Eve, but of any she knows about. Specifically there is some information about a boon Roy owes (ventrue who resides on the west side.<br /> <br /> 3. We are warned that Joe has connections and backing within the city by Octavia. We shouldn't rush to action. Further, the members of the council (who number about a dozen) have a mutual defense pact. It would be unwise to go off half cocked.<br /> <br /> So Alice and I resolve to investigate further before forming a slick plan to bring pain upon the house of Joe (the Dark Lord.) We are operating on vampire timescale after all. We need not rush to action.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Carthian Party</u></b><br /> <br /> We have been invited to attend a Carthian party by Terry the mekhet. Dorris Bettes is the one throwing it, but carthians are allowed to invite others to the party. Alice and I were invited by Terry, and Susan Small was invited by Kat (at my request.)<br /> <br /> The party would take place at the hidden speakeasy on the pier that Alice and I refurbished during our time in the kiddie pool. Since we left, the place has changed hands a few times, and in that time has grown. Whereas initially, the &quot;vampire hangout&quot; portion of the building solely included the hidden speakeasy. The building includes a bookstore and a movie theater, and now the book store's upper floor has been taken over as well. I do not know who exactly is responsible for this expansion.<br /> <br /> Anyway, as our group of revelers approached the bookstore, we noticed that Dorris had taken some precautions to keep mortals away tonight. At strategic intersections on approach to the bookstore are groups of intimidating looking groups of people.<br /> <br /> 1. Some hoodrats standing next to a car playing loud rap music.<br /> 2. Some &quot;working girls&quot; and their handler.<br /> 3. Some mean looking bums holding a jar of urine.<br /> <br /> To back this up was an aura of dread leaving the place feeling extra forboding. We think Dorris hired a nosferatu to keep the normals away.<br /> <br /> So, we head to the alley entrance where Dorris (daeva, Carthian) and Miles (Daeva, Carthian) are working the door. As we are conversing with them, Kyle (mekhet, childe of Simon) and Simon (Lance, Archon) arrive with about a half dozen ghouls and begin walking into the building (without a ticket.)<br /> <br /> Miles: &quot;Y-you can't do that. You need a ticket.&quot;<br /> Kyle turns to face Miles and says: &quot;We are mekhet, and we are here. to. Take.&quot;<br /> <br /> Dorris and Miles back off and the mekhet disappear into the building. Alice and I show our invitations and follow them. On the top floor in the old speakeasy, the Archon is questioning Patrick Brown (nosferatu, ordo dracul slave) while Kyle keeps the other kindred at bay.<br /> <br /> It seems that the Archon is looking for Darren Colville, a known associate of Patrick's. However, Patrick is extremely stubborn and won't tell the Archon how to cross the street, let alone where his friend is.<br /> <br /> Mid interrogation, the archon notices Alice and Me. He points his finger and speaks: &quot;You two. Wait for me on the roof.&quot; We comply.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>On the Roof</u></b><br /> <br /> We arrive on the roof to find the following kindred:<br /> <br /> Michael Seville (nosferatu priscus, elder)<br /> Archie (daeva, carthian)<br /> Earl Gossett (gangrel, carthian, the squirrel poacher from an early chapter)<br /> Steward Smiles (nosferatu, aspiring invictus)<br /> <br /> <b>Earl Gossett:</b> &quot;He can't do that. Elysium is there. Every kindred has a right to go to Elysium.&quot;<br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot;You are not being barred from Elysium, only from traveling in the personal territory of the Seneschal. If you want to attend Elysium, you will have to be escorted there by the keeper of Elysium or her designated agent.&quot;<br /> <b>Earl Gossett:</b> &quot;But you could talk to him, or take it to the council and overrule him, right?&quot;<br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot;We are not such good friends Earl, that I will oppose the Seneschal on this matter. But, your problems are much bigger than you realize. This is an invictus town, in case you haven't noticed. I think that very soon the other invictus landholders will follow the example of their elder and you will be barred from a lot more territory.<br /> <b>Earl Gossett:</b> &quot;That's Bullshit!&quot;<br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot;Mr. Gossett, you would be amazed at how many problems can be avoided by the application of manners.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Helicopter Parent</u></b><br /> <br /> Steward Smiles then asked to speak to Alice and Me privately. We walked to the other end of the roof and he explained that his childe (Patrick Brown, yes the same one the Archon is questioning) was having a hard time in the kiddie pool. Steward has been following him around using obfuscate.<br /> <br /> Currently, the kiddie pool is inhabited mostly by carthians and aspiring carthians. This is not surprising. As the SW territory gets squeezed by conflict with neighbors and overpopulation, some of them have been choosing to apply for citizenship of Baltimore.<br /> <br /> Anyway, some of the carthians have been beating Patrick up because he is a slave of the Ordo Dracul. They want him to tell them where the chapter house is, switch sides to the Carthians. (Alice and I didn't have a chance to look into this matter this session, but we will. Rest assured.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>A Message from the Archon</u></b><br /> <br /> At this point the Archon arrives on the roof. &quot;Everyone who is not a citizen of the city leave. now.&quot;<br /> <b>Seville</b> (looking a little annoyed): &quot;And what should the citizens of the city do?&quot;<br /> <b>Archon Simon:</b> &quot;Alder Seville, as always your company is welcomed. However, you may do as you please.&quot;<br /> Seville leaves, proving the point he was trying to make to Earl Gossett a few minutes ago.<br /> <br /> The Archon approaches Alice and Me and says: &quot;Your haven has been attacked. The haven of a mekhet of the city and of the Prince's bloodline. The perpetrators still live. Some delay could be seen as prudent. More delay will not be seen as genius. Take who you need, travel to their territory and enforce collective responsibility.&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, Alice and I take this as a go ahead to bypass our normal cautious pace. To make a long story short, a few nights later we gathered a posse of mostly Mekhet and Ventrue and traveled to Council territory. We captured Joe (the dark lord), his grandchilde (mike), and great grandchilder (Jenny, Missy, and Sherry.) Their torpid bodies were brought before the Archon Helen (crone) for final death... with one exception. Sherry was taken prisoner. Why? I'll explain later, but for now I'll say she is part of an evil conspiracy of Alice's and mine.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>The Wicked Tongue of Susan Small</u></b><br /> <br /> The main event at the party was supposed to be pot-luck talent show. The participants did not get to choose what talent they would display in advance. Instead, they drew a slip of paper from a hat about a week in advance. While we were waiting for the show to start, we listened in on a conversation Susan Small (ventrue, dragon, neonate, harpy) was having with a few kiddie pool residents.<br /> <br /> Theodore (nosferatu, carthian, kiddie pooler) was complaining about the unfair system the elders had put in place. Miles (carthian, daeva) Angela (carthian, daeva) and Delores (carthian, daeva ) all three kiddie poolers, were listening to Theodore and nodding in agreement. Theodore continues to opine that territories and feeding rights should apportioned according to vampire population and need.<br /> <br /> Well, Susan Small interjects into the conversation. &quot;All this is well and good, but the Elders do have the power and therefore they do make the rules.&quot; She continues, &quot;But, if you had the power you could make the rules. Tell me, how far would you be willing to go to get the power of the elders?&quot;<br /> <br /> Theodore: &quot;I would be willing to do whatever it takes.&quot;<br /> Miles, Delores, and Angela all agree with this sentiment.<br /> <br /> Susan: &quot;Whatever it takes, huh? Spider? Spider, will you join us please?&quot;<br /> Spider (carthian, nosferatu) joins the small group.<br /> Susan: &quot;Theoretically, if giving a blowjob to Spider would grant you the power of the Elders, would you do it?&quot;<br /> Theodore: &quot;Do what!?!&quot;<br /> Susan: &quot;Suck his dick. If performing fellatio on Spider would grant you the powers you seek, would you do it?&quot;<br /> Theodore sits there staring daggers at Susan as Miles, Delores, and Angela admit somewhat reluctantly that they would in fact give a BJ to Spider to acquire the power of the elders... theoretically.<br /> <br /> Susan: &quot;So, theoretically we have three powerful elders here, but in practice what we have here are two whores and a sexual deviant.&quot;<br /> <br /> Jaws drop and Susan walks off with a smug look on her face.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>The Talent Show</u></b><br /> <br /> There were only 2 performances of note.<br /> <br /> 1. Spider does a magic act in which he saws Auntie (daeva, carthian) in half. However, the box in which Auntie sat awaiting the saw was comically long, making it obvious Spider had no future as a stage magician.<br /> <br /> 2. Terry recited a poem. There were some jeers and catcalls when she took the stage. Here is what she read:<br /> <br /> &quot;The Mekhet's Poem&quot;, by Terry the Mekhet.<br /> <br /> On highways and byways the car engines sound<br /> They move in the dark, for Baltimore bound<br /> The Night will forever be making it plain:<br /> You have to defend what you want to maintain.<br /> <br /> So join our ranks and go through the Rite<br /> We always need kindred willing to fight<br /> With fire in our hearts, and stars in our eyes,<br /> We'll leave no trespassers under Baltimore skies!<br /> <br /> In the darkest of nights, when trust often dies<br /> Kindred walk safely under Baltimore skies;<br /> But some would destroy that in hopes to recall<br /> The chaos incarnate of all against all.<br /> <br /> Some people are parasites, taking their joy<br /> In friendships they ruin and hopes they destroy<br /> While some folks are builders, who hold in our hearts<br /> A dream that is more than the sum of its parts!<br /> <br /> Trespassers are poison; no trip is too far<br /> To hound them to death like the vermin they are!<br /> But they -are- good for one thing \u2014 the way that they cry<br /> When they realise it is their time to die.<br /> <br /> So join our ranks and go thourgh the Rite<br /> We always need kindred willing to fight<br /> With fire in our hearts, and stars in our eyes,<br /> We 'll leave no trespassers under Baltimore skies!<br /> <br /> We'll hunt them like dogs till the last of them dies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I still have a lot to finish writing up. More to come! I hope you have enjoyed reading this. Question and comments are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":64,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","user":"figurehead","date":". 02-15-2015, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T00:33:29-08:00","id":400102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/399664-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-actual-play-part-6#post399664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question and comments are welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also write that in my actual plays <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I never get them either... so I'm just responding to show you that at least 1 person has read your actual play <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Cheers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T02:31:20-08:00","id":400128,"title":"","content":"figurehead, where have you been? Long silence you had, I just thought my favourite Requiem actual Play had died out. Glad to know I was wrong!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T03:54:17-08:00","id":400164,"title":"","content":"&lt;&lt; Susan: &quot;So, theoretically we have three powerful elders here, but in practice what we have here are two whores and a sexual deviant.&quot; &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> No actually, in practice, there are three kindred who admitted that they consider sexual intercourse as a valid tool in the acquisition of power. (No surprise there, considering they were Daeva.) And someone who comes from a clan as inbred and incestuous as the Ventrue in Baltimore in that setting has no room to be throwing stones in the glass house of sexual perversion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T04:04:38-08:00","id":400166,"title":"","content":"Actually the cock-sucker-to-be was Nosferatu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T15:35:10-08:00","id":400898,"title":"","content":"Nice writeup, as always, and nicer still coming from Felix and Alice. Waiting for more. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T18:17:07-08:00","id":402686,"title":"","content":"@Griautus: Thanks for reading man! I'm glad to see your game has such longevity.<br /> <br /> @Thorbes: I'm glad to be back. Scheduling has been tough for the past couple months. Thanks for the kind words <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> @Audrey: It's not incest when WE do it!!! But seriously... I married outside the family :P<br /> <br /> @Phersus: Thanks for reading <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Wait no more. Here's another chapter.<br /> <br /> By the way, Terry's poem was adapted from the song &quot;Providence Skies&quot; by Cat Faber. Credit where credit is due. [<a href=\"http://catfaber.bandcamp.com/track/providence-skies\" target=\"_blank\">LINK</a>]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":64,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","user":"figurehead","date":". 02-11-2015, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T18:18:03-08:00","id":402689,"title":"","content":"<b><u>The Commissioner's Daughter</u></b><br /> <br /> One of the stops we made while gathering our posse was at the Von Berg Family estate. While there, we were approached by Darren Soderberg (my cousin.) Soberberg is the city Censor. It is his job to proactively seek out and prevent or seal breaches of the masquerade. Usually it's minor stuff that may or may not lead to a real breach. Tonight is different.<br /> <br /> Darren: &quot;There is a situation I need your assistance with.&quot; On the dining room table are photographs, maps, papers etc. &quot;Three girls have recently gone missing. One of them is the Police Commissioner's daughter. They've put their best investigators on this. Until the case is closed, there will be real police work going on. They will be shining their lights into the dark places our kind like to do their business.<br /> <br /> We are given a list of leads and sent to burn some shoe leather. Since Darren knows we have been operating in and out of Council Territory, we are sent there. Our investigation eventually leads us to a crack house where some cops are &quot;questioning&quot; a dood. With their fists. There are 2 cops in the basement where the suspect is tied up. There are three more in the garage rifling through the junk, and more still sitting in a few cars out front. There are far too many for Alice and I to subdue and dominate.<br /> <br /> Under cover of obfuscate, we travel to the basement, where Alice peruses the mind of the dood being questioned. His mind is a bit of a mess, but Alice is able to learn that the dood is a blood bound slave of a vampire, and while he does not know where the girls are being kept he does know that his master is involved somehow. He also knows the location of the local Elysium and a couple vampire havens. So far, the blood bond is keeping him from talking, but Alice and I are not confident he will be able to hold out forever.<br /> <br /> We withdraw and travel to the Council Elysium. Under normal circumstances, Alice would not use her auspex so casually, for legal reasons. All bets are off in this situation, and we are acting with the authority of the Baltimore Censor. So, Alice spends a goodly amount of willpower points to steal the information we seek from the minds of the local vampires.<br /> <br /> The commissioner's daughter and her friends are being kept in a seriously low class brothel. Alice and I travel there not only to confirm the story, but also to make sure there are no vampires on site presently. After all, we are about to send the cops there. When we arrive, we do see a vampire there. He is negotiating with the brothels owner for some time with one of the girls. He is offered some &quot;new product&quot; but declines. Alice and I wait for him to finish his meal without ever making our presence known.<br /> <br /> Satisfied that we have found the girls and there are no other vampires on the scene, we call Darren from a payphone. Darren in turn calls in an anonymous tip, and the cops who were questioning the blood slave split up into two more manageable groups.<br /> <br /> Having rescued the girls and being made heroes, the cops are happy to withdraw and resume their weekend. (it was saturday night.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>The Birdcage</u></b><br /> <br /> In the basement of our haven there is a birdcage. It is 2 meters tall, 1 meter in diameter, and is constructed of really thick steel bars. It has sat empty for far too long.<br /> <br /> Alice and I have been thinking for a while now that we needed some new servants. We are not interested in more ghouls, or even vampires who have sworn their loyalty or fealty to us. No, we want something more permanent. We want owned vampire servants. (Slave is such an ugly word for it.)<br /> <br /> We had recently been awarded a small patch of land in the Locust Point Industrial Area, and we would need agents to handle our business when we were away doing the cool kickass stuff we do. So, Alice and I put our heads together and made a list of all the vulnerable vampires in the city; the ones who had the least social protection. Then we discussed the list and decided that it would be good to choose servants who would not make the other jealous. In the end, we decided on Aika and Aiko (daeva, neonates, lancea sanctum, twins) That's right, they are twins. Hey, there are worse reasons to destroy someone's life and take their freedom.<br /> <br /> I will have to build a second birdcage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Stalkers</u></b><br /> <br /> So, Alice and I began stalking Aika and Aiko. To the best of our knowlege, their discipline spread is Celerity 3, Majesty 3 (we could be wrong) and their favorite game is cat and mouse. Throughout the years, we would often find them stalking their own victims. In the kiddie pool, they liked to lurk on rooftops, waiting for a vampire to be walking alone before pouncing on them. Later, after the NE territory of &quot;the Boss&quot; was cleared of vampires, we found them playing the same game with the new game warden there. After they learned of the Princes decree that all territories east of the city and north of Canton would be left fallow, they had moved their operation.<br /> <br /> We found the twins in the barrens which separate Baltimore from Council Territory. They were perched atop a water tower surveying the land. Alice and I waited patiently, and soon a vampire came walking down the railroad tracks toward Baltimore. The twins followed the vampire, and we followed the twins.<br /> <br /> The rail road tracks lead directly into the territory of the Lancea Sactum. The twins waited for the vampire to feed (poach) on their territory before pouncing on him. They beat him up and then let him go. Then they chased him again and beat him up again. This is their favorite activity.<br /> <br /> Alice and I continued to stalk the twins. We arrived in the barrens early in the night, waited for the twins to take up their perch atop the water tower and hunt their prey. I figured it would only be a matter of time before they would either make a mistake and need to be punished or make a mistake and need to be rescued. Either was fine by me.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Unexpected Visitors</u></b><br /> <br /> One night, while stalking the twins a vampire came walking down the rail road tracks. (council territory is seriously overpopulated. Even after the Dark Lord and his progeny were destroyed, they still have trouble feeding.)<br /> <br /> Anyway, Aika and Aiko are preparing to strike when two other people approach. They have predatory auras, but they do not feel like vampire auras... The bigger of the two dudes is currently holding the vampire by the throat and asking him, &quot;Where is your Alpha? Where is the Vampire Alpha of Baltimore.&quot; The poor vampire doesn't know. He is left with a concave chest and the two men continue moving toward Baltimore. Meanwhile, Aika and Aiko turned and ran away at the first sign of greater predators.<br /> <br /> Alice and I choose to follow them under cover of obfuscate. They continue moving east toward the bridge. Just on this side of the bridge is Alice's and my territory. Currently, our territory is unimproved. There are only two things of any importance there at this time:<br /> <br /> 1. A park bench under a tree.<br /> 2. A large murder of Crows who live in the tree. (I recently bought some animalism and invited the crows to live there. The deal is, they keep their eyes on the place for me, I dominate old men to come there and feed them on a daily basis.<br /> <br /> So, when the two cross into my territory, I move in closer and realize that I recognize the larger of the two men. I have met him twice.<br /> <br /> 1. A long time ago, I used Dominate to make a meal of him for Terry the mekhet near the movie theatre. She described his blood as being like fire (in a good way.)<br /> 2. I rescued him from being beaten by Elliot Jr. and his coterie during Pilgrim's golden ticket hunt.<br /> <br /> So, Alice and I appeared before him (a fair distance off) and asked to speak to him. He remembered me and was willing to talk. He tells me that a young member of his pack has been taken prisoner in the city and is being held captive by vampire magic. I ask him if he will let me look into the matter on his behalf in an effort to avoid violence. He tells me that he will sit on that bench until dawn. If she hasn't been returned to him by then, he will continue looking for her on his own.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Lost Dog</u></b><br /> <br /> Well... A few nights ago Alice and I saw the Archon trying to find Darren Colville by questioning Patrick Brown. We headed across the bridge to the Quarantine Zone looking for either or both of them. Here is how it went.<br /> <br /> 1. We spoke to Cooper. He is the almoner and is in this neighborhood pretty much all the time.<br /> 2. Cooper hasn't seen Darren in a long time, but knows that Patrick Brown has been spending a lot of time with Eve Liebsch lately.<br /> 3. We went to Eve's apartment, and Patrick was there.<br /> 4. We are able to get Patrick to speak after a few social rolls and an impassioned plea.<br /> 5. Darren has recently set himself up in a new haven in Little Venice.<br /> <br /> Little Venice is a shitty apartment complex on the water just south of Canton. It is in the Quarantine Zone, which also happens to be Michael Seville's territory. About half of the building has been condemned and has no electricity due to water damage from partially sinking into the bay. Alice discovers via auspex that an outsider has recently moved into the area. (most of the residents are chinese. a white guy moving in sticks out a little.) While walking the condemned portion of the building, we notice that one of the apartments has a new steel door installed.<br /> <br /> To make a long story short, Darren is unaware he is even in trouble. He has met a werewolf girl by coincidence and discovered that her blood is extra good and tasty. He has blood bound her to him and they are playing house together.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Uncommon Stupidity</u></b><br /> <br /> Because this all happened in the territory of Michael Seville, it was him to who we reported the incident. From there, we spoke to Antony (ventrue, invictus, sheriff.) Antony called Lance Kasson (daeva, invictus, sire of Patricia Mason.) Together, we travelled to Little Venice. There, Lance used his advanced knowledge of Majesty to convince Darren, his ghoul, and his wolf that it would be a great idea to go with him. Meanwhile, Alice and I spend some time cleaning up the memories of the more nosey residents of Little Venice.<br /> <br /> The Sheriff told us to meet him at Elysium when we were finished here. We did. There, we learned that there was a trial about to begin. We were handed hooded cloaks as we entered a room we had not yet seen. The city kindred were arranged in a theatre of the round. Next, about a dozen vampires whom we have never seen arrive in the room. They are all nude. They arrange themselves into a rather impressive throne. Next, the Prince arrives and seats himself upon the throne. Finally, Darren Colville is dragged into the room by Simon (mekhet, archon, lancea sanctum) and Helen (mekhet, archon, crone.)<br /> <br /> Darren tries and fails to speak several times. His mouth appears to filled with sticky tar or pitch or something. I am informed later by Alice that a telepathic conversation is taking place between the Prince and His Archons. One is acting as prosecutor and the other defender. The trial ends quickly. Darren Colville is convicted of the high crime Uncommon Stupidity. He is beheaded, and his head placed into a velvet bag, which is put into a box.<br /> <br /> The Prince departs the room. He is followed by his &quot;throne.&quot; Only then do the rest of us depart. The box is handed to Alice and me for delivery.<br /> <br /> We rush back to Locust Point to find that the werewolf is no longer sitting under the tree. I ask the crows where he went. They inform me that &quot;Two walking carrion arrived and attacked him. The fight went into that building over there.&quot; A short distance away is an abandoned warehouse, which are common in the LPI. We arrive to see two vampires whom we have never met, unconscious at the feet of the werewolf, who is surrounded by other werewolves who were apparently following the dood from twilight.<br /> <br /> He looks up: &quot;The veil must be maintained.&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;We will take care of it.&quot;<br /> Him: &quot;You will take responsibility? Fine.&quot;<br /> <br /> I breathe a sigh of relief and present him with the box. Soon after the wolf girl is delivered. The pack gather in a group embrace. Their Alpha sniffs her and confirms that she is no longer under the influence of vampire magic. We agree that there is no need for violence and that the matter is closed. The werewolf pack vanish from sight, leaving behind the head of Darren Colville.<br /> <br /> The box is burned, the bodies of Marco and Polo (who I learned are new members of the Quarantine Zone) are delivered to the sheriff for storage, and Alice and I go home for a well deserved nap.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Still not done with the write up. I should be able to get it done in the next day or two. Also, next game session is this Sunday. Thanks again for reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":64,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","user":"figurehead","date":". 02-11-2015, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T18:07:30-08:00","id":403941,"title":"","content":"<b><u>The Wrong Foot</u></b><br /> <br /> Since the Carthian Party, I have had a chance to speak to my youngest cousin, Susan Small. I wanted to find out why she was in such a bad mood. She told me that Bartholomew had awakened. He was sending her on all manner of mundane, time consuming errands. She warned me to stay scarce to face the same fate.<br /> <br /> Not long after, I did have to stop by the chapter house (I was looking for Enrique.) It was my plan to slip in and out as quickly as possible. However, no sooner did I open the door to the chapter house than I was intercepted by Bartholomew. He approached quickly, embraced me, kissed me on both cheeks and introduced himself.<br /> <br /> &quot;I am Bartholomew, Master of Equilibrium, Sworn of the Mysteries.&quot; I stood frozen in his embrace, waiting for the inevitable. It didn't come. Bartholomew didn't snatch me up and send us on time consuming errands. Instead, he wanted to thank me for my assistance during his torpor.<br /> <br /> In spite of the fact that Bartholomew has been in torpor since before I arrived in the city, we have had dealings with him and his childer in earlier chapters.<br /> <br /> 1. Alice and I, with the help of Kade and later Enrique had saved the torpid vampire from Belial's brood.<br /> 2. Alice and I had additionally freed his fledgling from a blood bond with Merry.<br /> 3. We had also made sure that his possessions (such as books, notes, etc) were moved to the chapter house for safe keeping.<br /> <br /> Bartholomew: &quot;I see a bright future for you. If there is anything I can do to assist you... Please. Just ask.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Alice and I left the chapter house a little bewildered. I didn't know what to think about this, but Alice did. Alice knew that we had been amassing a fair bit of political capitol of late. We had recently stopped a potentially serious breach of the masquerade, and defused a conflict with a werewolf pack before it even began. Now there is a Mystery Sworn Dragon who wants to reward us for past endeavours? Awesome. [Alice confirmed with the ST that we could trade these boons for things like City Status, Covenant Status, or even other stuff if we could think of it.]<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>The Taking of Aika and Aiko</u></b><br /> <br /> We couldn't jump the gun or tip our hands. More prep work would be needed. here is how we did it:<br /> <br /> 1. We had been given permission to look at Eve's ledger of boons. We learned that Theodore (nosferatu, carthian, kiddie pooler, all around asshole) had somehow gotten a major boon from Aika and Aiko. Apparently, the twins asked him for detailed information about the residents of Council Territory. They wanted to trade a minor boon for it, but Theodore convinced them that he could get himself in a lot of trouble with a lot of kindred for airing their dirty laundry. Well, the twins really wanted to go mess with them so they agreed.<br /> 2. Theodore had the boon in writing, and was willing to trade it to us, if we would arrange a haven for him. (remember, kiddie pooler's havens have no legal protections.) We agreed.<br /> 3. It just so happens that we know of a fully upgraded haven which has recently been vacated in Little Venice.<br /> 4. We paid a minor boon to Michael Seville in exchange for rights for Theodore to live there. When we brought him the keys that same night, he was impressed, and he gave us the boon.<br /> <br /> 5. We continued stalking the twins. Sure enough, they were continuing to mess with poachers from Council Territory. So, I decided to impersonate a poacher from Council territory, using Obfuscate powers. I walked along the railroad tracks in disguise, with Alice trailing me invisibly. When she informed me telepathically that the twins were on my trail, I altered my course and headed north toward the University (dragon territory.)<br /> 6. I had arranged for Scarlett and Robin (dragon slaves, gangrel, sisters) to be in the area in animal forms, as witnesses. Still disguised, I lured a frat boy into the shadows and fed from him.<br /> 7. After a few social rolls [expression and subterfuge] I was attacked by the twins. Alice didn't agree with this part of the plan. She was pissed at me when I let Elliot Jr beat me up that one time, and she was pissed off at me this time too. I wasn't too worried though. If things got out of hand, Scarlett, Robin, and Alice were all present.<br /> <br /> 8. We spoke to Calypso (daeva, crone, childe of the Priestess) and asked her if we could bring some guests to receive the blessings of the Crone. She wanted more information and we informed her that we would be inviting Aika and Aiko to the celebration. Aika and Aiko are members of the Lancea Sanctum, so Calypso wasn't so sure we were thinking straight. We assured her that we could make it happen. We also had to promise her that we were doing what we were doing for selfish reasons. We promised. &quot;Then, we will accept your sacrifice.&quot;<br /> <br /> 9. We spoke to Enrique (ventrue, dragon, axe sworn.) We asked him to waive his right of first choice of victims and spoils. We explain the situation and he agrees in exchange for a minor boon. We also speak to Susan. She has the most access to our Grandsire Konrad out of all of us. We ask her to ask him not to interfere in this case. &quot;You owe me for this.&quot;<br /> <br /> 10. We invited Aika and Aiko to meet us at Elysium. There, we produced the written boon we had bought from Theodore. &quot;We knew that was a mistake... What do you want?&quot; We invite them to attend the next Crone Ceremony on the new moon and receive the blessings from the Priestess.<br /> <br /> Aika: &quot;Please, not that. Can't you think of some other service we can perform?&quot;<br /> Aiko: &quot;We can do so, so many things for you.&quot;<br /> <br /> The twins know that boons are enforceable in Baltimore. Further, if they do not cooperate and other vampires have to help force them to comply, they will then owe boons to each and every vampire who &quot;helped&quot; them fulfill their obligations. That is the reason Alice and I chose to do this publicly, with as many witnesses as possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>The Cookie Jar</u></b><br /> <br /> First, Alice and I went to see Bartholomew. We asked him if we was willing to help us out. He still was. We told him that I had been attacked while feeding on Dragon territory by members of the Lance, and we brought witnesses. Bartholomew feigned shock, and after Scarlett and Robin had left, asked us what we want. He told us that he could bring a grievance to the seneschal on behalf of the covenant, but that it would not be easy because the Lance was unlikely to allow one of their members to be condemned to slavery.<br /> <br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;If you wait but a fortnight, we have arranged for their covenant protections to be lifted temporarily.&quot;<br /> <b>Bartholomew:</b> &quot;You're making it easy to help you.&quot;<br /> <br /> The night before the next new moon, Alice approached Simon (mekhet, archon, lance) and asked him if he would speak on our behalf and tell the seneschal how helpful She and I had been with regard to the recent werewolf problem.<br /> <br /> That same night, I went to see Darren Soderberg (ventrue, invictus, censor, my cousin) and asked if he would speak on our behalf to the Seneschal and tell him how helpful Alice and I were in the recent prevention of a masquerade breech.<br /> <br /> <b>Darren:</b> &quot;Did you do something bad? Are you trying to avoid punishment?&quot;<br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;No. We want a cookie.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Springing the Trap</u></b><br /> <br /> Aika and Aiko did indeed show up to the ceremony. We watched as they participated in all the rituals and were blessed with the blasphemous powers of the Crone. They didn't leave until we were satisfied. We know from experience, that walking around smelling of blasphemy will generally get you temporarily shunned by the church. Under normal circumstances, in about a month the blessings would wear off and things would return to normal.<br /> <br /> So, the next night there is a line leading to the office of the Seneschal:<br /> <br /> 1. Simon the Archon<br /> 2. Darren the Censor<br /> 3. Alice and Me<br /> 4. Bartholomew the Mystery Sworn<br /> <br /> When Alice and I entered the office, Peter looked up: &quot;I was wondering when the two of you would make an appearance.&quot; We reiterated our recent service to the city and informed him that Bartholomew would arrive shortly to file a grievance. &quot;We do not ask you to rig the trial, but if you do rule in favor of our covenant, we ask that you award the lives and freedom of Aika and Aiko to the covenant.&quot;<br /> <br /> There is a hearing over which the Seneschal presides. The defense of Aika and Aiko goes something like this: &quot;We didn't know it was him, and anyway we were trying to help the police poachers.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Bartholomew:</b> &quot;We extend travel rights through our territory as a courtesy to citizens of the city. We neither ask for, nor require the assistance of others to police our territories in this way. Additionally, how our members choose practice the masquerade and move amongst the herd unnoticed is a matter of personal choice.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Seneschal rules in favor of the Ordo Dracul and orders that &quot;the lives, freedoms, and liberty of Aika and Aiko are the property of the Ordo Dracul.&quot;<br /> <br /> Later, at the chapter house, Bartholomew rules that as I am the aggrieved party, the award should go to Alice and me. Two lives for two lives. Whatever boon he thought he owed me, is paid.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>A word on Clan Daeva</u></b><br /> <br /> You might be wondering: WTF? Why doesn't the Priestess protect her clanmates? Well, as it turns out, clan Daeva is at somewhat of a disadvantage in the city. Appolonia is something of an absentee landlord to her clanmates. I don't have in character confirmation, but it is my belief that she is blood bound to the prince. Further, this action weakens the Lancea Sanctum by some degree. I think the Priestess of the Crone will be OK with that. As for Pilgrim (archbishop of the Lance) I am hoping that he will use this as a cautionary tale for his flock (see what happens when you stray from the church?) rather than rallying the faithful to fuck with us.<br /> <br /> Either way, Alice and I are going to steer clear of Church lands.<br /> <br /> So there you have it. Now all we have to do is find the twins, capture them, and put them in the bird cage, right? RIGHT??<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This should bring the story up to date. Hope you enjoyed it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The next session is this Sunday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":64,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","user":"figurehead","date":". 02-12-2015, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T12:12:28-08:00","id":404885,"title":"","content":"Is the Lancea Sanctum so bloated with excess laity that they don't bother with evangelical activities and are fine with two apostate Dragons enslaving not one but two of their members, as well and forcibly converting them into worshipping the Crone? Not spending excessive status capital and boons on them is one thing, but for the Church to say and do nothing is a sign of weakness on their part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","user":"Audrey St. John","date":". 02-13-2015, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T16:52:34-08:00","id":405284,"title":"","content":"Aika and Aiko were not enslaved by two apostate dragons. At least not officially. They were enslaved by a court of Baltimore presided over by an Invictus Elder. At this point, only the Prince Himself could overrule this decision. I have no doubt that the unofficial truth will come out. Vampire society is a low privacy society, after all.<br /> <br /> Will there be consequences? I'm sure there will be. I don't honestly know what they will be, but we did choose Aika and Aiko in no small part because they had little social protection in the city. Since thevery beginning of the game, the two of them had been very insular; shunning the company of most others. While they did attend mass on the regular, it was my impression that their faith was less in Longinus and more in the opportunities to &quot;be a better monster&quot; and &quot;punish the wicked&quot; that the church afforded them.<br /> <br /> Out of character, when Alice and I were discussing with the ST ways to get our hands on the twins there were other, less risky plans proposed.<br /> <br /> Example 1: Pilgrim (archbishop) has had a political alliance with my Uncle Septimus since before the game began. We could have approached either or both of them and said basically &quot;we are on board with this alliance and will support it. However, we will need a pair of 'loyal attendants' to act as liaison between us and the church.&quot;<br /> <br /> Example 2: Michael Seville hates the church. Really hates it. We could have gone to him and said &quot;we are on board with your plan to weaken the church. We will help you further that goal to its logical conclusion and... if during that course an opportunity comes up to take slaves you could support us.&quot;<br /> <br /> Example 3: We could push for a war between covenants and ride into battle with the Axe Sworn. In which case there would be opportunities to choose slave and spoils and what not.<br /> <br /> As for the relative strength of the Church in Baltimore, it's tough to say for sure. However, Pilgrim is certainly in weakest position of all the elders. The Prince is a seriously powerful individual. The remaining Elders consist of His oldest friend (Michael Seville), His oldest ally (Konrad Von Berg), His childer (Peter), His blood bound thrall (Appolonia), and... Pilgrim. Pilgrim is a relative newcomer to the city. He does not have the kind of ties that the other elders do.<br /> <br /> As for numbers, the non-Invictus covenants have between 8-11 members. The Dragons, which at the beginning of the game had barely enough kindred to form a coterie now have 11 members and a fair number of slaves in the kiddie pool just waiting to bolster our numbers. Invictus currently has 22 members.<br /> <br /> I haven't seen a lot of evangelism from the Church, but a big reason for that is I convinced Preacher to leave for New York. Preacher was a Lance member who showed up in my kiddie pool days, and I wrote about him in an earlier chapter. He would have been very good for the church. He was a good fighter, charismatic, knew theban sorcery, etc. He was on a mission to destroy Belial's Brood wherever it could be found. We convinced him through both word and deed that Alice and I were willing and able to watch after Baltimore, so he could move on.<br /> <br /> So, Alice and I have been chipping away at the church for a while now. But you are right, Alice and I are not going to be the favorite vampires of the church. We will have to keep our eyes peeled for reprisals, and be on our best legal behavior.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T04:26:34-08:00","id":405692,"title":"","content":"This is such a well realised game. Its really cool how Felix and Alice have developed. In the earlier parts of the game, the courts and legal system of the city was something to be feared but now you understand it enough to twist it to your own sordid advantage. You also write really well, you provide the proper context for whats going on without getting too bogged down in detail. This is great.<br /> <br /> I have a few questions about the game if you have the time to answer them.<br /> <br /> Are you guys using any of the 2E rules at all? It seems touchstones and even humanity wouldn't have much of a place in your game as it stands.<br /> <br /> This game has a lot of NPCs and lots of them seem really fleshed out with character and motivations. How does your storyteller present the NPCs? Does he/she give detailed descriptions or do some of the quirks come about from the storyteller acting the characters mannerisms? What do they do to make them so vivid?<br /> In my games I have successfully created a few well fleshed out NPCs over time but nothing like the scale of what you guys seem to have done in your game. Any tips on this is done would be really appreciated!<br /> <br /> How much of your game's plots comes from freeflow game and how much is planned out ahead of time by the Storyteller? The plots and subplots seem to mesh really well that its not clear how much of anything is planned out (even roughly) and how much comes from your ST adlibbing.<br /> <br /> Finally, any update on the wyrm's nest you guys found in the game? That subplot doesn't seem to have come up for a little while, any movement on it? I really liked the map finding dynamic.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T19:06:28-08:00","id":408476,"title":"","content":"@Gravitas Man: I'll try to answer your questions in order.<br /> <br /> 1. For the most part no. We are not using the 2E rules. We are using some though. I would describe our game as Requiem 1.1.<br /> <br /> We have been ignoring the humanity rules as they are written since as far back as I can remember. We do use humanity as a roleplaying tool, nothing more. For example, Alice and Felix both have humanity 5. Why? Because the players chose it. We do our best to roleplay as vampires with that humanity level.<br /> <br /> Were the humanity rules made better than before with 2E? Yes, absolutely. But still not good enough that I think they would make the game more fun. The main reason is that our group prefers to play long running games where the consequences of one's actions play out socially. As opposed to a game where doing naughty things leads to downward spiral inevitably leading to the PCs becoming unplayable.<br /> <br /> 2. Regarding NPC's: Well... first we feel that NPCs are THE most important part of setting up a game. Playing in a game with few NPCs or poorly crafted NPCs in akin to playing in a desert and not very much fun. According to my ST: &quot;the NPCs ARE the game.&quot;<br /> <br /> It is important for the PCs to have some sort of emotional connection to as many NPCs as possible. This doesn't mean they have to like and be friends with them. Hating an NPC is just as valuable as loving them.<br /> <br /> Some tips for creating good NPCs include:<br /> <br /> a. A good introduction. It can be easy as an ST to just bring the PCs to a gathering of NPCs, state that the NPCs are clumped into a few groups, and have the PCs just walk up to each group and say &quot;Hi, my name is...&quot; over and over.<br /> <br /> It is better to include in the introduction scene for an NPC some action that tells the players something about that character. So, right away the NPC in question is more than just a cardboard cutout named Bob. It is Bob the vampire whose jealousy and desperation led him to sabotage Jim the vampire. Or something.<br /> <br /> This doesn't mean that you have to do this for every single vampire at the aforementioned gathering. Just realize that just because a given NPC was in the scene, and may even have shook hands and exchanged names with the PCs doesn't necessarily mean they were introduced. Make plans for a proper introduction at some later date.<br /> <br /> b. Good NPCs should have motivations and stuff to do. If the PCs have the impression that whenever they leave the room the NPC ceases to exist until such time as they come back, this is a bad thing. One easy place to start here is to think of the sorts of things PCs have done in previous games you have played in or ran and assign similar motivations to some NPCs.<br /> <br /> c. schrodinger's box: My ST will often have a few general ideas about NPCs but not commit to them until the last moment. Just like schrodinger's cat, you never know the status of the cat till you open the box.<br /> <br /> d. Pictures help. They help both the ST and the Players to imagine the NPC and their place in the world.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 3. Regarding the game plots. I know that my ST does plan out some things in advance of each game. He generally doesn't plan it in such a way where it's like &quot;the PCs will do this or that.&quot; It's more like, &quot;X will happen.&quot; and from there he thinks about who will care about &quot;X&quot; and what they might do about it. So even if Alice and I don't get involved in &quot;X&quot; it still affects the city and we will probably hear about it sooner or later from the lips of the harpies. If we do choose to get involved, he already knows who is likely to be involved either as ally or adversary.<br /> <br /> The players often plan things in advance of the game as well. We generally will give the ST a heads up during the week if we have something we want to do in the game and how we plan to approach it.<br /> <br /> In addition to the stuff the ST plans and the PCs plan, there is a fair amount of off the cuff stuff that happens. But because my ST has done such a good job of making the city and it's NPCs (he knows who lives where, and what sort of stuff they are likely to be doing) it is easier for him to mesh what we are doing into the fabric of the story of Baltimore.<br /> <br /> 4. As for the wyrm's nest, it should come as no surprise that the nest in question had already been discovered and was known to Quintus, and probably other members of the covenant. I am told by the ST (out of character) that there are other nests in the city, but Alice and Felix have yet to find any.<br /> <br /> I haven't pursued the map quest any further. The ST told me that if/when we do, we will learn a lot about the history of the city. However, the next clue is somewhere in Appolonia's garden. Even with the goodwill we think we have with the Circle of the Crone in general and Appolonia in specific, we are afraid of the prospect of digging around in the garden of the Priestess of the Crone. I do intend to pursue the maps in the future, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":64,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","user":"figurehead","date":". 02-21-2015, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T21:48:43-08:00","id":413732,"title":"","content":"@Audrey: I got a chance to ask my ST more about why we were allowed to capture two members of Lancea laity.<br /> <br /> 1. You might remember one of the earliest stories from the game in which we assisted Mandy O'Kelly as she defiled a holy site. The ritual she used was called &quot;the sacrifice of the king.&quot; The long and short of it was she chose a mortal and treated him like a king for a year and a day before stringing him up by his ankles and bleeding him slowly at the holy site (library.)<br /> <br /> Apparently, Pilgrim (archbishop) had sent Aika and Aiko into the kiddie pool with orders to prevent the blasphemy. So, the twins had almost a year to figure out what was going on. They could have easily taken the &quot;king&quot; away from Mandy O'Kelly at some point during the year. Instead, they showed up at the last minute and made a half-assed attempt to get past Alice and me. As I recall, we stabbed one of them in the stomach and they both fled. They brought Lucien Du Lac with them (thereby outnumbering us 3 to 2) and still ran. Lucien fled soon after, but at least he had the excuse that he was then outnumbered 2 to 1.<br /> <br /> Since exiting the kiddie pool, the twins have spent most of their time as I have detailed above rather than working to better the church. So, Aika and Aiko didn't exactly have high covenant status.<br /> <br /> 2. According to ST, in the mind of Pilgrim the twins (daeva) belong just as much if not more to Appolonia (daeva priscus.) He thinks that if the Daeva priscus showed up and used some of her Majesty powers on the twins it wouldn't be too hard for her to steal the twins from the church. So, in Pilgrims mind the capture of the twins weakened the Daeva Priscus more than it weakened the church.<br /> <br /> 3. Alice and Felix have twice now repelled attempts by Belial's Brood to probe the defenses and/or invade Baltimore. I don't know if pilgrim knows about the first, but he certainly knows about the events aboard the Esperanza. There was also the time when Alice, Spider, and I rescued Dorothy (pilgrims's grandchilde, lancea sanctum member) from a vampire attack outside the city when we were returning from one of our trips to New York. This has earned Alice and Felix a certain amount of goodwill from the church and from Pilgrim.<br /> <br /> Anyway, my ST informs me that we have burned away whatever goodwill we had left and are now closer to &quot;neutral/distrust&quot; with many members of the church.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":64,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","user":"figurehead","date":". 02-21-2015, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T03:09:25-08:00","id":413937,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your response figurehead. Happily, I do follow a largely similar process to your ST when it comes to making NPCs. I think working on good introductions is something I'll take on board (and this can easily roll over into story hooks) and maybe have what the &quot;off-stage&quot; NPC actions be more noticable or have the repurcussions be felt more. Actually thinking about it, my most successful NPCs, especially the villianous ones have had a strong introduction, so thats something I'll actively plan out in the future.<br /> <br /> I'm looking forward to reading what comes next.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T18:33:42-08:00","id":422385,"title":"","content":"Before I do the next write up, I wanted to give a little background information to make the game a bit easier to understand, starting with a little geography. [<a href=\"http://s10.postimg.org/rwkq78urd/Geography.png\" target=\"_blank\">LINK</a>]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Carthian Territory</u></b><br /> <br /> All of the Carthian Territories within the city of Baltimore are held by Michael Seville (nosferatu priscus.)<br /> <br /> 1. The main Carthian holdings. Everything north of the dotted line is overseen by Dorris Bettes.<br /> 2. Federal Hill - Not much action has happened here over the course of the game. I have heard rumors that Seville is looking to sell or trade this territory.<br /> 3. The Quarantine Zone (not to be confused with the kiddie pool - which is the orange territory on the inner harbor.) The Quarantine Zone is where new vampires go to be tested for rabies. Some of the more obvious character flaws can be identified and the vampires who suffer them culled before they even enter the kiddie pool for their real test.<br /> <br /> At the south end of the Quarantine Zone are the storage garages where new vampires are first dropped off. Also at the south end is the Butcher shop where Cooper (Daeva, almoner) rations out animal blood.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Locust Point Penninsula</u></b><br /> <br /> Construction and development is underway on Locust Point. A few chapters back, territories were assigned to neonate coteries for homesteading. The territories were assigned as follows:<br /> <br /> A. Alice and Felix's coterie<br /> B. Darren Soderberg's Coterie<br /> C. Dorris Bettes' Coterie<br /> D. Lucien Du Lac's Coterie<br /> E. Spider's Coterie<br /> <br /> The coveted metro station was originally meant to be built right in the middle of Dorris' territory. She put herself in no small amount boon debt to get that territory. In reality, my uncle Septimus worked behind the scenes to have the metro station moved at the last minute. Now, it will be located on the border territories A and B closer to the bridge. Dorris' territory will be landlocked and mostly surrounded by my family.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Outlands</u></b><br /> <br /> On the west of the map, you will see the territories of the Council and of Roy, which have been on the forefront of the story lately.<br /> <br /> On the east of the map everything between the Quarantine Zone (3) and Sevilles main holdings (1) which is colored in shades of brown and gray have been declared fallow by the prince. So, no vampires are allowed to haven, feed, or gather mortal influence there. We can travel trough, but nothing more. he exception to this rule is the Game Warden who lives there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Carthian Politics</u></b><br /> <br /> At the start of the game, the Sheriff Elliot Rex was a very influential Carthian. He was really the only check to the power of Michael Seville within the covenant. However, once it was learned that he was the my Sire's murderer, we engaged in a conspiracy to see him killed. Now that he is gone, Michael Seville is the only Carthian landowner and the only Carthian older than a neonate.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Dorris Bettes (daeva, carthian, neonate) is very concerned that Michael Seville will be the next Prince. In fact, she thinks he would make a terrifying dictator and feels that time is running out before his position becomes unassailable.<br /> <br /> It is for that reason that Dorris went to council territory a few chapters back and encouraged some of them to Immigrate to Baltimore. It was the equivalent of poking a small hole in a dam. There was a small number of immigrants at first, and they have come in waves. First came the idealists, then came the opportunists. I don't know what's next, but I know that Council Territory is overpopulated with vampires, and both the Quarantine Zone and the Kiddie pool are heading in that direction too.<br /> <br /> In fact, Dorris would rather see my Uncle Septimus (invictus) become Prince than Michael Seville. Why? Septimus isn't so powerful that he can rule as an absolute dictator. Therefore, the various powers of the city will be able to influence his decisions. Therefore, pluralism.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Near Future</u></b><br /> <br /> Elliot Jr is back in town and causing trouble. He acted via cat's paw during last week's game. When I get a chance to write a full update I will fill you all in.<br /> <br /> The forseeable future of the game will involve dealing with the Quarantine Zone and Kiddie Pool (ie: culling the bad ones, mentoring the good ones, separating the joiners from the invaders, etc.) After that, I believe the game will focus on the neonate coterie homesteads in Locust Point (ie: developing the territories, disagreements with neighbors, poachers from the Quarantine Zone, etc.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>On the Horizon</u></b><br /> <br /> Because there are not vast tracts of wilderness between cities on the east coast, there is easier travel and conflict between them. For a while now, my ST has been foreshadowing a future in which we return to New York to help my Great Uncle Adhamar become Prince not just of the Bronx, but of all New York.<br /> <br /> Also, I believe Belial's Brood have established a foothold in Philadelphia and corrupted the Lancea Church there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Next game is Sunday. Hopefully I'll have a chance to write up the past two sessions this week sometime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T02:00:35-08:00","id":424971,"title":"","content":"First, let me say I've absolutely enjoyed reading this story so far. This is a great, well realized Chronicle. I particularly admire the balance between the Clans and the Covenents as important organizations. When I first signed on to Requiem, I didn't give two hoots about Clan. Pfft, who your born into? Whatever, it's a stat spread. Your Covenent is who you chose, so they are what is important! Having the heavy emphasis on family in this game has proven to me that Clan can and should be important to a game. Your storyteller has done a fantastic job of bringing their NPCs to life and deserves a lot of credit. Also, you and Alice's player deserve a lot of credit as well, because the best game in the world can't be saved from players who won't embrace it and play it. My next vampire is likely to be inspired in part by Felix's strategies for gaining influence.<br /> <br /> Now, a couple of questions. <br /> <br /> Posted on June 3, 2014, on page 4, the Prince called the whole city in to ask them to fight. He then gave control of the city for the night to Peter, the Seneschal. In that you mention, &quot;Soon, a young man with hair of blonde ringlets entered the room. There was no mistaking that this was the Prince. This was also the first time I had laid eyes upon him without an obfuscate disguise.&quot; I was wondering about that. How did you know that this was his actual form without an obfuscated disguise? And for that matter, he's always appeared before wearing a disguise. Why do you suppose that this time he showed up 'in the flesh' so to speak?<br /> <br /> From what we've read here, I get the feeling that a lot more play seems to happen around the Ventrue than it does amongs the Mekhet. Is this a byproduct of you reporting more on what Felix is more active in, and there are adventures of Alice (the most awesomest Mekhet ever) that we don't hear about? Or is there a 'bias' towards the Ventrue half of the marriage? Or, am I perhaps just misreading the whole thing so far? That's a possibility I'm sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1744-thantrax","name":"Thantrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T18:08:49-08:00","id":425902,"title":"","content":"@Thantrax: Thanks for the compliments <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's always great to hear that people other than me are enjoying the write-up.<br /> <br /> As for your questions:<br /> <br /> 1: At the time when I wrote that, I was pretty sure I was looking upon the true face of the Prince. I reasoned that in the presence of so many of the citizens of Baltimore (some of them decades/centuries older than me) that many of them would have at some point seen the true face of the Prince and therefore any charade would fail. I now see the folly of this reasoning.<br /> <br /> Over the course of the chronicle, I have seen the Prince wear many faces. Most recently, he appeared at a mekhet meeting (Terry's first) appearing like a statue of Apollo; all marble perfection. So, I really have no clue as to what the true appearance or even gender of the Prince might be. I have a feeling that Konrad Von Berg, Michael Seville, and Peter know, but they're not talking.<br /> <br /> 2. I would say that more play happens in proximity to the ventrue side of the family for a few reasons:<br /> a. The PCs just like hanging out with my cousins a bit more.<br /> b. The Mekhet are meant to be seriously mysterious. So, the ST is a little more careful about the planning and timing of meetings and actions of the Mekhetocracy.<br /> <br /> Also, because the write-up is written from the perspective of my PC, Felix I wind up writing a little more about the things that stick more vividly in my mind. Alice's PC tends to play a little more low key game than me, and when the focus is on her she is likely to be sneaking around spying on people which doesn't translate into long exposition :P<br /> <br /> Thanks again for your kind words and questions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T18:20:21-08:00","id":425933,"title":"","content":"A long time ago now, I sold Caroline Key to the Keeper of Elysium in exchange for her permission to create new Official Elysium venue to be run by my cousin Christina. Out of character, I have been trying to think of cool ideas for the place. I have an idea that I think is adequate, but I am not in love with it. Does anyone have an Idea for a cool Elysium run by ventrue neonates? If so, please share and I will recommend it to Christina at the next game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T03:55:08-08:00","id":426414,"title":"","content":"That depends on whom you want to cater to really.<br /> <br /> A smoking parlor (So many different themes can be used for decor.)<br /> A card room (not to be confused with a casino)<br /> A bowling alley<br /> An indoor golf course (May or may not include putt putt or disc golf)<br /> A trampoline park (I suspect your setting's master of elysium may shoot that down as too tacky though.)<br /> A convention center/sports arena large enough to cater to multiple college level or semi-professional teams and acting troupes, comedians etc. but too small for performers like Beyonce etc.<br /> A laser tag/paintball arena. (May get vetoed as tacky or a violation of the spirit of Elysium.)<br /> 'Buy' a yacht and use it to hold dinner parties and dances and special events (like a guest interactive faux murder mystery) while cruising around the harbor for a few hours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","user":"Audrey St. John","date":". 03-03-2015, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T09:21:17-08:00","id":426631,"title":"","content":"Seems to me the best thing to do with a permission like this is to see how you can make it do double duty. Elysium isn't just a cool place to hang out, it's also kinda a social bullet proof shield. It seems to me that if one has the option to pick an Elysium, one might be well served to place it at some place that someone might want to protect. <br /> <br /> Idea 1 : If you could somehow make it possible, a post office would be f*ing great. Especially if that could be put in the Quarantine Zone and/or Kiddie Pool. Remember how Felix gathered a boon by agreeing to store documents in a safe spot? What safer spot than a safety deposit box in an Elysium? By placing it in the Kiddie Pool, you give all those young, needy vampires a place to store their valuables where the other young needy vampires won't swipe them. It's also a foolproof way for their sires to discretely funnel supplies to their kids inside the pool, and guarantee they get them. Variants on this could be FexEx or a bank, but I suspect getting approval for those would be just as difficult or even more. The downside to this is that there isn't much of a hoppin' social scene inside of the local post office, but it would be a good neutral meeting ground and it's easy to think of a reason you need to go there.<br /> <br /> Idea 2 : This one might be a hard sell with the master of Elysium, but maybe if done right... An underground street fighting arena. Provides good entertainment for the masses. Lots of people there means that you can have a meeting with someone and not be worried about being overheard. You might even be able to spin that into being a location where people hold their Kindred duels when people feel that occasional need, as Felix himself has twice now. One could make it known that those fighters that people are seeing fight are available for snacks later. If Caroline has access to Dominate 3, she could let paying Kindred customers pick out which burly ball of violence they'd love to feed from and then make them forget the whole thing after. Feeling a bit light headed after a match wouldn't be out of place. The downside to this one would of course be that it's not exactly... legal. Police could possibly be a problem.<br /> <br /> I love Audrey's suggestion of a yacht. A moveable Elysium sounds like it could be awesome, and it plays to the unique nature of the Pool, it being a dock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1744-thantrax","name":"Thantrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T18:21:08-08:00","id":432087,"title":"","content":"Thanks Audrey and Thantrax for the ideas. I bounced some of them off the group. The yacht idea was shot down due to money/logistics issues. The current frontrunner is an old hotel converted to apartments. I don't have all the minutia figured out, but I'm thinking there will be certain apartments what share walls with the kindred meeting place which will be observable by a kindred audience via 2 way glass or hidden cameras or something.<br /> <br /> We will use the mortal inhabitants of these apartments to put on &quot;puppet plays&quot; as detailed in the invictus 1e covenant book. Further, we will make the &quot;actors&quot; available to snack on for a price. Imagine watching your favorite TV show and being able to send out for your favorite character.<br /> <br /> I have also kicked around the idea of a vampire version of &quot;the Dollhouse.&quot; Because our family has a monopoly on Dominate in Baltimore, why not use our power to create custom memory/personality setups and charge kindred for the privilege of playing with our dolls?<br /> <br /> Anyway, the next game is a week away and I still have a lot of material to write up from the last few sessions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T02:23:57-07:00","id":433727,"title":"","content":"If I were you, I'd lean towards the one way mirror approach. It would likely be more comfortable for the Elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1744-thantrax","name":"Thantrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T03:59:01-07:00","id":433780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thantrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/399664-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-actual-play-part-6?p=433727#post433727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were you, I'd lean towards the one way mirror approach. It would likely be more comfortable for the Elders.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the first VtR story arcs I role played in was inspired by Dark City and kind of drifted into the Fantasy Island/Dollhouse premise. It's an unnecessary breach of the Masquerade that can quickly and easily spiral out of control. Because Felix and Co. believe his family has an exclusive monopoly on Dominate (that may not actually be true considering the number of unknown elements drifting in and out of the setting) so Felix's family can't claim plausible deniability and blame anyone else for their indiscretions. But hey, have fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","user":"Audrey St. John","date":". 03-09-2015, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T18:35:35-07:00","id":437836,"title":"","content":"That's good advice Audrey, and you're absolutely correct that there are unknowns that drift in and out of the setting. To top that off, the ship has sort of sailed on the whole ventrue dominate thing. Roy, who oversees one of the border territories is a Ventrue. I'm not sure if he is a citizen of Baltimore or just a vassal of Baltimore, and I'm not sure how much it matters one way or the other. For better or worse there he is. I think Septimus' plan would work better in a different part of the country. On the east coast, cities blend together for hundreds of miles. It's not like traveling vampires would find themselves in the middle of the country with no food or shelter like they might if the game was set in say... Denver Colorado or Anchorage Alaska.<br /> <br /> But yeah, Felix is feeling pretty cocky lately and he might get spanked. On the other hand, we need something to differentiate our Elysium from the others. It can't just be another place to sit and talk. We need to give kindred a reason to go there, and a reason to spend their money (boons) there.<br /> <br /> One idea I had was to outfit some of the rooms as highly secure, highly luxurious havens. Perhaps kindred would pay for the privilege of sleeping in a genuine Elysium, with all the protections that implies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":64,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","user":"figurehead","date":". 03-11-2015, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T02:00:20-07:00","id":439627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/399664-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-actual-play-part-6?p=437836#post437836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One idea I had was to outfit some of the rooms as highly secure, highly luxurious havens. Perhaps kindred would pay for the privilege of sleeping in a genuine Elysium, with all the protections that implies.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a truly great idea, but beware if any of your guests gets murdered while in her sleep, as the consequences would be terrifying for Felix and Alice. To say the truth, i've always thought of Master of Elysium as a punishment, not a boon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}